# 15. Feature Engineering

Traditional Machine Learning often required humans to identify useful features.

For example, if we want to classify images, the computer ultimately receives numerical pixel information.

Humans may try to identify useful characteristics:

```text
Shape
Edges
Texture
Color
Patterns
```

These characteristics can become features for the model.

The problem is that complicated problems can contain enormous numbers of useful patterns.

Manually designing all of them becomes difficult.

This is one reason neural networks became important.

