## Final Summary

The lecture connects **Forward Deployed Engineering** with the evolution of AI.

An FDE's job is to take a **real-world problem**, understand it deeply, convert it into a proper requirement, choose an appropriate technical solution, build it, and help bring it into production.

The AI portion explains why we moved from:

```text
Explicit Rules
```

to:

```text
Machine Learning
```

then:

```text
Neural Networks
```

then:

```text
RNNs
```

and finally:

```text
Transformers
```

which enabled modern:

```text
Large Language Models
        ↓
Generative AI
```

The most important concept is that modern AI is not simply a collection of manually written `if/else` rules. Modern models **learn patterns and relationships from large amounts of data**, and Transformers use **attention** to model relationships within context.
